<div id="S3.SS2.SSS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS2.SSS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">The mathematical formulations underlying our adaptive federated learning system are defined as follows:</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.SSS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="S3.E3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(3)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="H_{t}=\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}(\alpha D_{stat}^{i}+\beta D_{arch}^{i}+\gamma D_{res}^{i})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>H</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false" rspace="0em">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mi>α</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow><mi>i</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>β</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow><mi>i</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>γ</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msubsup><mi>D</mi><mrow><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow><mi>i</mi></msubsup></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">H_{t}=\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}(\alpha D_{stat}^{i}+\beta D_{arch}^{i}+\gamma D_{res}^{i})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.SSS2.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="S3.E4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(4)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{t}^{*}=\arg\min_{C_{t}}\mathcal{L}_{global}(C_{t})+\lambda_{1}\mathcal{R}_{comm}(C_{t})+\lambda_{2}\mathcal{R}_{fairness}(C_{t})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>C</mi><mi>t</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>arg</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><munder><mi>min</mi><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>t</mi></msub></munder></mrow><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mrow><mi>g</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>b</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>m</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><msub><mi>λ</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℛ</mi><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{t}^{*}=\arg\min_{C_{t}}\mathcal{L}_{global}(C_{t})+\lambda_{1}\mathcal{R}_{comm}(C_{t})+\lambda_{2}\mathcal{R}_{fairness}(C_{t})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.SSS2.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="S3.E5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(5)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="w_{i}^{fair}=\frac{\phi_{i}+\epsilon}{\sum_{j=1}^{N}(\phi_{j}+\epsilon)}\cdot\frac{1}{1+\delta\cdot\log(|D_{i}|)}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>w</mi><mi>i</mi><mrow><mi>f</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>a</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>r</mi></mrow></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mrow><msubsup><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>j</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><mrow><mo lspace="0em" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>ϕ</mi><mi>j</mi></msub><mo>+</mo><mi>ϵ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>δ</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">w_{i}^{fair}=\frac{\phi_{i}+\epsilon}{\sum_{j=1}^{N}(\phi_{j}+\epsilon)}\cdot\frac{1}{1+\delta\cdot\log(|D_{i}|)}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.SSS2.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="S3.E6" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(6)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{k}^{t}=\text{softmax}((t-\tau_{k})/\sigma_{k})" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>π</mi><mi>k</mi><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>softmax</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>τ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>/</mo><msub><mi>σ</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{k}^{t}=\text{softmax}((t-\tau_{k})/\sigma_{k})</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.SSS2.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="S3.E7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(7)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="M_{multi}^{t}=\text{CrossModalFusion}\left(\sum_{m=1}^{M}\alpha_{m}\cdot E_{m}(X_{m})\right)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msubsup><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>l</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>t</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>i</mi></mrow><mi>t</mi></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>CrossModalFusion</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><munderover><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>m</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>M</mi></munderover><msub><mi>α</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mi>E</mi><mi>m</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>X</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">M_{multi}^{t}=\text{CrossModalFusion}\left(\sum_{m=1}^{M}\alpha_{m}\cdot E_{m}(X_{m})\right)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.SSS2.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="S3.E8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(8)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{M}(D)=\text{Clip}(\nabla F(D))+\mathcal{N}(0,\sigma^{2}I)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℳ</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mtext>Clip</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mrow><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>F</mi></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>D</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒩</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><msup><mi>σ</mi><mn>2</mn></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>I</mi></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{M}(D)=\text{Clip}(\nabla F(D))+\mathcal{N}(0,\sigma^{2}I)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.SSS2.p8" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="S3.E9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(9)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{Load}_{i}(t)=\frac{\text{Compute}_{i}(t)}{\text{Capacity}_{i}}\cdot\text{NetworkDelay}_{i}(t)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mtext>Load</mtext><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><mfrac><mrow><msub><mtext>Compute</mtext><mi>i</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><msub><mtext>Capacity</mtext><mi>i</mi></msub></mfrac><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><msub><mtext>NetworkDelay</mtext><mi>i</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>t</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{Load}_{i}(t)=\frac{\text{Compute}_{i}(t)}{\text{Capacity}_{i}}\cdot\text{NetworkDelay}_{i}(t)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.SSS2.p9" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="S3.E10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_left"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_left">(10)</span></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S3.E10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta_{consensus}=\text{ByzantineRobust}(\{\theta_{i}\}_{i=1}^{N},f)" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>θ</mi><mrow><mi>c</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>o</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>e</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>n</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>u</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>s</mi></mrow></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>ByzantineRobust</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><msub><mi>θ</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup><mo>,</mo><mi>f</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta_{consensus}=\text{ByzantineRobust}(\{\theta_{i}\}_{i=1}^{N},f)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.SSS2.p10" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS2.SSS2.p10.1" class="ltx_p">Table <a href="#S3.T4" title="Table 4 ‣ 3.2.2. Core Mathematical Framework ‣ 3.2. Mathematical Foundations and Theoretical Guarantees ‣ 3. Vision: Adaptive, Fair, and Scalable Federated Learning ‣ Beyond Static Knowledge Messengers: Towards Adaptive, Fair, and Scalable Federated Learning for Medical AI" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> summarizes the core mathematical components driving our adaptive federated learning system. Each formulation addresses specific healthcare challenges while maintaining theoretical rigor and practical applicability.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.SSS2.p11" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS2.SSS2.p11.1" class="ltx_p">The <span id="S3.SS2.SSS2.p11.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Heterogeneity Index</span> (Equation (<a href="#S3.E3" title="In 3.2.2. Core Mathematical Framework ‣ 3.2. Mathematical Foundations and Theoretical Guarantees ‣ 3. Vision: Adaptive, Fair, and Scalable Federated Learning ‣ Beyond Static Knowledge Messengers: Towards Adaptive, Fair, and Scalable Federated Learning for Medical AI" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>)) combines statistical data distribution differences, architectural model variations, and resource computational constraints to provide real-time network state assessment. The <span id="S3.SS2.SSS2.p11.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Adaptive Capacity</span> (Equation (<a href="#S3.E4" title="In 3.2.2. Core Mathematical Framework ‣ 3.2. Mathematical Foundations and Theoretical Guarantees ‣ 3. Vision: Adaptive, Fair, and Scalable Federated Learning ‣ Beyond Static Knowledge Messengers: Towards Adaptive, Fair, and Scalable Federated Learning for Medical AI" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a>)) optimization balances global learning effectiveness with communication costs and fairness requirements through multi-objective optimization. <span id="S3.SS2.SSS2.p11.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Fairness Weighting</span> (Equation (<a href="#S3.E5" title="In 3.2.2. Core Mathematical Framework ‣ 3.2. Mathematical Foundations and Theoretical Guarantees ‣ 3. Vision: Adaptive, Fair, and Scalable Federated Learning ‣ Beyond Static Knowledge Messengers: Towards Adaptive, Fair, and Scalable Federated Learning for Medical AI" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>)) employs Shapley values to ensure equitable contribution recognition while reducing data volume bias that typically favors large institutions.</p>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS2.SSS2.p12" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS2.SSS2.p12.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.SS2.SSS2.p12.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Curriculum Progression</span> (Equation (<a href="#S3.E6" title="In 3.2.2. Core Mathematical Framework ‣ 3.2. Mathematical Foundations and Theoretical Guarantees ‣ 3. Vision: Adaptive, Fair, and Scalable Federated Learning ‣ Beyond Static Knowledge Messengers: Towards Adaptive, Fair, and Scalable Federated Learning for Medical AI" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>)) implements structured knowledge transfer that introduces complexity gradually, reducing communication rounds through intelligent sequencing. <span id="S3.SS2.SSS2.p12.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Multi-Modal Fusion</span> (Equation (<a href="#S3.E7" title="In 3.2.2. Core Mathematical Framework ‣ 3.2. Mathematical Foundations and Theoretical Guarantees ‣ 3. Vision: Adaptive, Fair, and Scalable Federated Learning ‣ Beyond Static Knowledge Messengers: Towards Adaptive, Fair, and Scalable Federated Learning for Medical AI" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">7</span></a>)) creates unified representations across imaging, genomic, EHR, and sensor data through cross-attention mechanisms. <span id="S3.SS2.SSS2.p12.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Privacy Mechanisms</span> (Equation (<a href="#S3.E8" title="In 3.2.2. Core Mathematical Framework ‣ 3.2. Mathematical Foundations and Theoretical Guarantees ‣ 3. Vision: Adaptive, Fair, and Scalable Federated Learning ‣ Beyond Static Knowledge Messengers: Towards Adaptive, Fair, and Scalable Federated Learning for Medical AI" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>)) provide formal differential privacy guarantees suitable for healthcare regulations while maintaining learning utility.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S3.F1" class="ltx_figure"><img src="2510.06259v1/figures/solution_architecture.png" id="S3.F1.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_square" style="aspect-ratio:476/398;" width="476" height="398" alt="Refer to caption">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure"><span id="S3.F1.3" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Figure 1</span>. </span><span id="S3.F1.4" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:90%;">Comprehensive Architecture for Adaptive, Fair, and Scalable Federated Learning in Healthcare. The system features hierarchical coordination, dynamic messengers, multi-modal data integration, and comprehensive privacy-fairness enforcement across all layers.</span></figcaption>
</figure>
